<body>
    <h1>Use Case 2.1.6.4: Admin Configures Mail Server for Creates Campaign=
 Setup (Step-4)</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p><strong>User Story</strong></p>
<p>As an Admin, I want to configure the mail server for a phishing simulati=
on campaign by selecting an available mail server from the list or configur=
ing my own mail server, so that I can send phishing emails through the chos=
en mail server.</p>
<p><strong>Description</strong></p>
<p>This use case outlines the process by which an Admin either selects an e=
xisting mail server from the list or configures their own custom mail serve=
r for use in a phishing simulation campaign. The Admin can preview the deta=
ils of an existing mail server and input the required configurations for th=
eir own mail server. After setting up the mail server, the Admin proceeds w=
ith the campaign setup. The mail server must be correctly configured for em=
ail sending to ensure proper delivery of phishing emails.</p>
<p><strong>Actors</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Admin</strong>: Selects a mail server from the list or configure=
s a custom mail server.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong>: Displays the list of available mail servers, al=
lows for custom mail server configuration, validates inputs, and saves the =
mail server configuration.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Preconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Admin is logged into the platform and has access to the <strong>Create N=
ew Campaign</strong> wizard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin is at the <strong>Mail Server Configuration</strong> step in t=
he campaign creation process.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays a list of <strong>Available Mail Servers</strong> as=
 well as the option to <strong>Configure Your Own Mail Server</strong>.</p>=
</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Postconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The selected or configured mail server is saved and available for use in=
 the phishing campaign.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can proceed to the next step in the campaign setup after confi=
guring the mail server.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Main Flow (Normal Success Scenario)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: Navigate to Mail Server Configuration</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin navigates to the <strong>Mail Server</strong> configuration st=
ep in the campaign creation wizard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays a list of <strong>Available Mail Servers</strong>, w=
hich are preconfigured mail servers the Admin can choose from.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 2: Select a Mail Server </strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin can choose an available mail server from the list (e.g., <stro=
ng>Client Office 365</strong>, <strong>Client Exchange Server</strong>, etc=
.).</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin clicks the <strong>Preview</strong> button to view the configu=
ration details of the selected mail server.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays the mail server's details in a preview window, showi=
ng the <strong>Server Address</strong>, <strong>Domain</strong>, <strong>Tr=
ansport</strong>, <strong>Port</strong>, Username, Password (password shoul=
d show in hidden) and the <strong>Mail Server Status</strong> (Active/Inact=
ive).</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can view whether the server is active and check its configurat=
ions (e.g., <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"http://smtp.office365.com" r=
el=3D"nofollow"><strong>smtp.office365.com</strong></a>, <a class=3D"extern=
al-link" data-card-appearance=3D"inline" href=3D"http://microsoft.com" rel=
=3D"nofollow">http://microsoft.com</a> , <strong>SMTP</strong>, <strong>Por=
t 587</strong>).</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can select the <strong>Close</strong> button to exit the previ=
ew and confirm the mail server selection.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin clicks the <strong>Save</strong> button to save the custom mai=
l server configuration.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 3: Confirmation and Exit</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>After the mail server configuration is completed (either by selecting an=
 existing server or adding a custom one), the system confirms that the mail=
 server is ready for use in the phishing campaign.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can click <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> to proceed to t=
he next step in the campaign creation process.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 4: Configure a Custom Mail Server</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>If the Admin decides to configure a custom mail server, they click on th=
e option to <strong>Configure Your Own Mail Server</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>A modal window opens, prompting the Admin to enter the required configur=
ation details:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Mail Server Name</strong>: The name of the custom mail server (e=
.g., <a class=3D"external-link" data-card-appearance=3D"inline" href=3D"htt=
p://office365.com" rel=3D"nofollow">http://office365.com</a> ).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Description</strong>: A brief description of the mail server (e.=
g., <strong>SMTP server for client=E2=80=99s Office 365</strong>).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Server Address</strong>: The mail server's address (e.g., <a cla=
ss=3D"external-link" href=3D"http://smtp.office365.com" rel=3D"nofollow"><s=
trong>smtp.office365.com</strong></a>).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Domain</strong>: The domain associated with the server (e.g., <a=
 class=3D"external-link" data-card-appearance=3D"inline" href=3D"http://mic=
rosoft.com" rel=3D"nofollow">http://microsoft.com</a> ).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Transport</strong>: The transport protocol used for the connecti=
on (e.g., <strong>SMTP</strong>).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Port</strong>: The port used for the mail server connection (e.g=
., <strong>587</strong>).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Username</strong>: The username for authenticating the mail serv=
er (e.g., <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"mailto:admin@office365.com" re=
l=3D"nofollow"><strong>admin@office365.com</strong></a>).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Password</strong>: The password for the username (encrypted for =
security).</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can also choose to test the mail server connection by checking=
 the <strong>Test Mail Server Connection</strong> box before clicking <stro=
ng>Save</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system validates the inputs to ensure that all required fields are f=
illed.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 5: Test Mail Server Configuration</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>After entering the mail server details, the Admin clicks the <strong>Tes=
t Mail Server Connection</strong> button.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system attempts to connect to the configured mail server to verify t=
he settings.</p></li>
<li>
<p>If the connection is successful, the system displays a message: "Mail Se=
rver Connection Successful".</p></li>
<li>
<p>If the connection fails, the system displays an error message and prompt=
s the Admin to check the configuration.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 6: Save Mail Server Configuration</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Once the custom mail server is successfully configured and tested, the A=
dmin clicks the <strong>Save</strong> button to save the configuration.</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p>The system saves the custom mail server configuration and makes it avail=
able for use in the phishing campaign.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 7: Proceed to Next Step</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>After saving the mail server configuration, the Admin can click <strong>=
Save &amp; Continue</strong> to proceed to the next step in the campaign cr=
eation process.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Frontend Form Validation</strong></p>
<p><strong>Field Validation Rules</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Mail Server Name</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: The Admin must provide a valid name for the=
 mail server.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Mail Server Name is required."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Server Address</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: The Admin must enter a valid mail server ad=
dress (e.g., <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"http://smtp.office365.com" =
rel=3D"nofollow"><strong>smtp.office365.com</strong></a>).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Server Address is required."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Domain</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: The Admin must enter a valid domain (e.g., =
<a class=3D"external-link" data-card-appearance=3D"inline" href=3D"http://m=
icrosoft.com" rel=3D"nofollow">http://microsoft.com</a> ).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Domain is required."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Transport</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: The Admin must select a valid transport pro=
tocol (e.g., <strong>SMTP</strong>).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Transport is required."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Port</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: The Admin must enter a valid port number (e=
.g., <strong>587</strong>).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Port is required."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Username</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: The Admin must enter a valid username for t=
he mail server.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Username is required."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Password</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: The Admin must enter a valid password (encr=
ypted for security).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Password is required.=E2=80=9D</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Business Rules</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"5b=
72da49-afa2-4294-ab50-e5cbd64829ac" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Rule</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-1</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The Admin must select an available mail server or configure a custom mai=
l server for the campaign.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-2</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>If the Admin configures a custom mail server, the <strong>Mail Server Na=
me</strong>, <strong>Server Address</strong>, <strong>Domain</strong>, <str=
ong>Transport</strong>, <strong>Port, username </strong>and<strong> passwor=
d</strong> must be provided.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-3</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The Admin can <strong>Preview</strong> the mail server details before se=
lecting it for the campaign.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-4</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Mail Server Status</strong> must be displayed for each avail=
able mail server (Active/Inactive).</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-5</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The Admin can choose a mail server from the list or configure their own =
mail server using the <strong>Configure Your Own Mail Server</strong> optio=
n.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-6</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The Admin must provide all necessary details (Mail Server Name, Server A=
ddress, Domain, etc.) for configuring the custom mail server.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-7</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can test the mail server connection before saving the configuratio=
n.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-8</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system ensures that only <strong>Active</strong> mail servers can be=
 selected for use in the campaign.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-9</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must click <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> after selecting or=
 configuring a mail server to proceed to the next step.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-10</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Test Mail Server Connection</strong> option is available for=
 custom mail servers to verify the connection before saving.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"9e=
68d8f2-b5c8-4669-a7fd-c2cf67794861" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Pass/Fail Condition</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-01</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can view a list of available mail servers.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Available servers are displayed correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-02</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can preview the configuration details of a selected mail server.</=
p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Mail server details (Server Address, Domain, Port, username, passwordetc=
.) are shown.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-03</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can configure a custom mail server by entering the necessary infor=
mation (Name, Server Address, etc.).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Custom mail server configuration is successfully saved.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-04</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select a mail server from the list and use it for the campaign=
.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The selected mail server is saved for the campaign.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-05</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can choose to configure their own mail server by clicking on <stro=
ng>Configure Your Own Mail Server</strong>.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can configure a new server.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-06</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can <strong>Preview</strong> the mail server configuration before =
selecting it.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Preview details are displayed correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-07</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can save the mail server configuration (either selected or custom)=
.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The mail server configuration is saved and ready for use.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-08</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system validates the mail server configuration inputs (Name, Address=
, Domain, etc.).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Validation messages are shown for any missing or incorrect inputs.</p></=
td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-09</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can cancel the configuration process and return to the previous st=
ep.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Clicking <strong>Cancel</strong> exits the process without saving any ch=
anges.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-10</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can view the <strong>Mail Server Status</strong> (Active/Inactive)=
 for each available mail server.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Mail server status is displayed correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-11</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can add a custom <strong>Mail Server Name</strong> for the server =
configuration.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
