<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>System Behavior &amp; Validation</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Mail Server List</strong>: Displays available preconfigured mail=
 servers for selection.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Custom Mail Server Configuration</strong>: Admin can manually in=
put server details if needed.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Preview</strong>: Admin can view detailed configuration before f=
inalizing the mail server.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Mail Server Status</strong>: The system displays whether the sel=
ected server is active or inactive.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: All fields (Name, Address, Domain, username=
, password etc.) must be validated before saving.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Security Handling</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Mail Server Details Security</strong>: All mail server configura=
tions must be securely stored.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Inactive Servers</strong>: Inactive servers cannot be used for p=
hishing campaigns, ensuring integrity.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Data Protection</strong>: Any configurations or data submitted m=
ust comply with security and privacy standards.</p></li>
</ul>
